  "truth_boundary": "The ChatGPT-to-Actions command bus is live-verified. The private Kim Dataverse queue and its v2.2 processor are live-reachable, but production reuse of the legacy approval secret is intentionally quarantined. The statically verified FO-GAS v2.3 successor removes plaintext approval requirements from owner-only dry-run execution, rotates ScriptProperties without returning the secret, scrubs approval columns and leaves live mutations disabled; it remains STAGED_NOT_DEPLOYED until a provider-capable Apps Script source update route is available. Google Cloud management and WIF mutation remain provider-gated. Canonical GitHub truth is controlled by the private last-admitted-commit pointer because provider-native branch protection is not exposed. The JARVIS benchmark central task module is a source candidate restricted to the committed public fixture, no network, no durable writes and no provider effects; registration on main, deployment and private evidence benchmarking remain unproven."
